  "id": "mesocortical-system",
  "term": "mesocortical system",
  "definition": "The mesocortical system is described here as a dopaminergic reward pathway that ends in parts of the frontal cortex such as the orbitofrontal cortex. In this context, it refers to a brain system involved in reward-related activity in the frontal region.",
